rs.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nPreserve public-to-private task dependencies on the private side, so plan graphs and `task deps` from either end retain ordering without exposing the private task’s identity on the public destination. Copying a home includes its members’ tasks and carries these edges onward; repeated copies keep one edge and remove stale entries. Unreadable private dependency records fail reads and copies instead of silently losing edges.\n\n## Why\n\nDeclaring ExampleOrg’s Linear private protects repository names, but previously let public rollout tasks run before their private prerequisites finished. Plans spanning both organizations need to retain dependency order without being split or ordered by hand.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe home’s existing member-project links remain unchanged.","created_at":"2026-10-15T12:49:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T15:17:53Z","closed_at":"2026-10-15T15:53:54Z","merged_at":"2026-10-15T15:53:54Z","merge_commit_sha":"f33a1dd50c4880128544377e27b559326f3de196","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":nu