l":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nBoth Linear live lanes reuse four owned document slots in ordinary CI while retaining update, read, filtering, metadata/Markdown and asset-recopy coverage. Fresh creation and deletion coverage runs daily, with transport-journal budgets of zero document creations per warm ordinary pass and four per daily pass.\n\n## Why\n\nPrevent Linear’s retained-trash quota from blocking unrelated changes or forcing replacement of the nominated test team, while preserving meaningful real-service coverage and deterministic protection against increasing daily document creation.\n\n## Additional info\n\nOrdinary CI initializes only missing standing slots before running reuse assertions. Those creations are journalled separately as a cold rebuild, outside both pass totals. Manual dispatch remains available for initialization and recovery. Ambiguous ownership, unverifiable team membership and uncertain create acknowledgements fail closed. Standing CI documents and their parent projects survive cleanup and the janitor.\n\nOrdinary, initialization and daily CI writers share a concurrency group with `cancel-in-progress: false` and `queue: max`; machine-local Session exclusivity remains. Local runs explicitly opt in with `ONETASKGRAPH_LINEAR_DOCUMENT_MODE=initialize`, exercise reuse assertions and retire their separately stamped set, including after failed initialization. Default local ordinary runs refuse an absent or incomplete set before writing.\n\nThe approved trade-off moves fresh creation and deletion assertions to daily coverage. See the [assertion inventory](docs/linear-document-assertion-inventory.md) and [lifecycle and privacy guidance](docs/linear-live-cleanup.md). Deleting documents does not restore quota. Budget reporting reads both lanes’ recorded HTTP journals without rerunning scenarios, counts subsequently deleted creations, reports cold rebuilds and failed-pass residue separately, and rejects missing or incomplete telemetry. Replay fixtures use synthetic content rather than captured workspace listings or private bodies.\n\nLabelled live task writes retry the specific `cannot resolve label …: found 0 matches` refusal within a bound, preserving that refusal if visibility never settles. Offline HTTP journeys cover delayed visibility, exhaustion and preservation of active labels through standing-set preparation, residue clearing and a second queued pass. This supports label-filter lag as an explanation but does not establish the cause of the earlier live failure.\n\nThe asset journey addresses the stale-read failure seen in [the required Ubuntu check](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/40972765063/job/123793400052): each invocation supplies distinct source content and waits boundedly for that content after copying. An HTTP replay reproduces a destination read holding the previous pass’s content after reset, preventing an incorrect unchanged-copy result from leaving the reset marker in place. No successful credentialed Linear rerun is claimed.\n\nThe offline asset replay now reuses HTTP connections at both ends, addressing loopback connection pressure implicated in [the required Windows check’s request-send failure](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/40982402040/job/123825424738). The credentialed live observer is unchanged; a successful Windows rerun is not claimed.\n\nAn incidental Python SDK test fix addresses double rounding in the import-measurement assertion that failed [the earlier required Ubuntu check](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/40950313486/job/123716544115). It compares the quoted three-decimal median with the reported four-decimal value using the rounding tolerance; the measurement script and the rest of the SDK are unchanged.","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:16:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T03:39:27Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T03:39:25Z","merged_at":"2026-10-30T03:39:25Z","merge_commit_sha":"3791687d504b5eb4866349d8cf7382e68fa8ede8","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3821/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3821/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3821/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/0c9fa8c795e01faacd6465e9b25fe4ba17773906","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/3819/bound-linear-documents","ref":"nick/3819/bound-linear-documents","sha":"0c9fa8c795e01faacd6465e9b25fe4ba17773906","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":