om/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3818/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/58ae137d9843d18209f438edcf8c80937e44067f"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":{"enabled_by":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"merge_method":"squash","commit_title":null,"commit_message":null},"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3804","id":5053920814,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUBBgxs8AAAABLTy2Lg","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3804","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3804.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3804.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3804","number":3804,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(github-projects): file a private home's public task in a private repository","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nPrivate GitHub Projects homes can now hold mixed public/private plans. New canonical issues naming a public repository use the project issue’s repository or configured fallback, while retaining their named repository and neutral public views. The board and actual issue repository must verify private; unreadable visibility refuses the write, and existing issues never move.\n\nEach copy reads each destination’s visibility once before its first write, independently of overlapping copies. Loopback CLI journeys cover placement, refusals, retries and updates; the visibility budget enforces one read per destination per command across separate project and document copies.\n\n## Why\n\nMixed plans previously failed when copied to a private GitHub home, forcing users to split their plans or keep approval local. This lets one private home hold the complete reviewed plan while exposing public work only through its screened views.\n\n## Additional info\n\nVisibility changes during a copy are detected by the next copy. Canonical issues remain in private repositories and reach done through their own status writes, mirrored to their public views; public-repository closing lines do not close them.\n\nThe recording proxy’s connection check accommodates unused client connections on Windows while still rejecting extra board connections. The overlapping-copy journey synchronizes at the HTTP response boundary to avoid a mutation racing its visibility assertions.","created_at":"2026-10-28T16:23:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T12:57:35Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T12:57:32Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T12:57:32Z","merge_commit_sha":"0203e9e5a53486a6d6acdec0a6cc2140a80674e2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3804/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3804/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3804/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/2e59ae574c78c66058d87b75fb2b3af7b9521583","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/3800/store-private-placement","ref":"nick/3800/store-private-placement","sha":"2e59ae574c78c66058d87b75fb2b3af7b9521583","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscript