ts): serialize CLI wheel builds that share a target directory","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nSerialize CLI-wheel builds across release and distribution paths with one shared lock on Linux, macOS and Windows. Release packaging and verification retain the lock while consuming shared output; failures release it for the next build.\n\n## Why\n\nBoth paths run in required pull-request checks, so their race randomly blocks unrelated work. Coordinating access fixes the cause of maturin’s missing-file failures instead of relying on retries until CI turns green.","created_at":"2026-10-29T02:15:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T04:27:36Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T04:27:34Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T04:27:34Z","merge_commit_sha":"9e027b6ba1c6d158c12b0c54c44c09a85954fb69","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3817/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.gi