":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nFix local Markdown root containment so Windows path spelling differences—verbatim prefixes, letter case and short names—do not falsely refuse project copies. Use filesystem identity when spellings disagree, while continuing to reject paths outside the root.\n\nAdd concurrent project-copy regression coverage and containment tests for Windows spellings; preserve the existing budget test’s refusal assertions.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows failure blocks the release carrying the fix for private Linear plans losing their public task projections, which the user’s host needs adopted. Fixing the store’s false refusal addresses the user-facing defect and removes the release blocker without relying on retries.","created_at":"2026-10-28T05:27:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T06:34:57Z","closed_at":"2026-10-28T06:34:56Z","merged_at":"2026-10-28T06:34:56Z","merge_commit_sha":"fb00886c7c6526b01c17d5fa92ec0ad5e56f96ba","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_