_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nAdd `project copy --member <ID>... --members-only`, exposed in both SDKs, to copy named tasks into an existing destination project without comparing, rewriting or reporting that project. If a required project counterpart is missing, refuse before writing and show the command that creates it.\n\n## Why\n\nSupport copying named members into an existing project while leaving the project itself alone.\n\n## Additional info\n\nBreaking Rust API change: the exhaustive public enums `CopyScope` and `EngineError` gain `MembersOnly` and `NoProjectCounterpart` variants, respectively.\n\nCloses #3084","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:57:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T10:00:05Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T10:00:05Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e352514dfdfc37742dfa43cbc72575dbdde88c7e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3717/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3717/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderoberti