d}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-23T00:02:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T23:21:48Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-01T00:47:19Z","git_url":"git://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:nickderobertis/onetaskgraph.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph","homepage":null,"size":16538,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":127,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":127,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3717"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3717"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3717"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3717/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3717/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3717/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/f41f708d199f2c187e99dc744cdbbaa8b364dbdf"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3714","id":4958005078,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUBBgxs8AAAABJ4UnVg","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3714","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3714.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3714.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3714","number":3714,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(copy)!: copy named members into an existing project without reading or writing the project","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nAdd `project copy --member <ID>... --members-only` to copy named tasks into an existing destination project without reading it for comparison or writing it. Missing counterparts fail before writes and name the full project-copy command needed to create them. Python and TypeScript SDKs expose the option; existing copy modes retain their behavior.\n\n## Why\n\nAdding a task mid-run should not require reading and mirroring destination project fields to protect its title, body, labels and metadata. This removes that workaround and its extra comparison reads from callers such as onepipeline write-back.\n\n## Additional info\n\nBreaking Rust API change: the exhaustive public enums gain `CopyScope::MembersOnly(CopyItems)` and `EngineError::NoProjectCounterpart`; downstream exhaustive matches must handle them.\n\nThe scope preserves member-copy dependency resolution, `delivered` and per-item `via`, and skips the orphan walk. Added journeys cover local Markdown, the GitHub loopback board, SDK calls, routing and rollback. GitHub task creation still performs its existing parent-context read; the new scope eliminates project comparison reads.\n\nMerged the image-asset changes from #3713 at `51c5f2b3`, preserving both features’ TypeScript tests. At merge commit `f41f708d`, the rebuilt binary passed all 45 TypeScript client tests with isolated configuration; format, lint and TypeScript type checks passed. Judged diff lint against `51c5f2b3` passed with history `20261022T062038Z-826ff`, zero findings. Broader acceptance journeys were not rerun for this merge resolution.\n\nEarlier verification at `a227cdc7`: `just lint-llm-diff origin/main` passed with history `20261021T221039Z-59491`: 19 passed, 0 failed, 22 skipped, 2 ignored, 13 not relevant.\n\nAn earlier macOS publication failed in `a_task_the_search_index_never_reports_ends_the_wait_at_its_bound_naming_that_task`: its diagnostic read occurred after 3.599211416 seconds against a 3-second wait plus 500 milliseconds for diagnosis. See the [failing macOS job](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/39671753325/job/119473030372) and [required aggregate job](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/39671753325/job/119513903103). Neither that test nor its timing bounds changed in the members-only implementation against base `7e616f93` at `a227cdc7`.\n\nAfter compiling the plugin and live fixture executables, the exact test passed alone with `cargo test --quiet -p onetaskgraph-github-projects-e2e --all-features --locked --test live_pair a_task_the_search_index_never_reports_ends_the_wait_at_its_bound_naming_that_task -- --exact` (1 passed, 12 filtered out; 8.97 seconds). The initial local invocation stopped before the timing assertion because the plugin fixture executable had not been compiled. The timing issue is recorded as follow-up `drafts:Verify--then-resolve--every-accepted-non-crozier-follow-up-ticket/drafts/20261021T221025Z-macos-fixture-timing-assertion-exceeds-diagnosti`.\n\nThe field-scoped `invalid_states_unrepresentable` suppression at `ProjectCopyArgs::members_only` is retained because Clap requires a member at parse and conversion constructs nonempty `CopyItems`; the boolean follows the CLI boundary’s existing flag representation. No suppressions were added during merge resolution.\n\nCloses #3084","created_at":"2026-10-21T20:36:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T09:57:07Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T09:51:31Z","merged_at":"2026-10-22T09:51:31Z","merge_commit_sha":"49cc9076115e891084b87602cba1e47be414d5e2","a