com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3644"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3644"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3644/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3644/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3644/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/802a8dbea72881e0c8d61f235874f6e4622c1b21"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3601","id":4836549129,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUBBgxs8AAAABIEfiCQ","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3601","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3601.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3601.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3601","number":3601,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci(macos): consolidate coverage and release builds","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nConsolidate macOS checks and installation proofs into one CI job, preserving protected check names and Linux/Windows coverage. Limit automatic scheduling to one Mac job per workflow run and two Mac-spending runs per single-push lifecycle, with release products verified before Linux publication.\n\n**Intel macOS artifacts are discontinued from the next release.** Apple Silicon remains supported; all other released platforms, the npm launcher, both SDKs and independent crate tags remain.\n\n## Why\n\nThe five-runner macOS pool is shared across repositories. Repeated platform jobs occupy scarce slots, leaving otherwise green changes and dependent releases queued. Consolidating existing proofs and builds returns capacity to other changes.\n\n## Additional info\n\nScheduling changes take effect on merge. Intel macOS discontinuation takes effect with the next release. No release was cut and branch protection was not edited.\n\n### Scheduling before and after\n\nBaseline: `31c5e024` (v0.7.0). Finished head: `a31084f1`, the merge of `main` at the v0.7.1 release (`31392146`) onto `b7e72bea`; it includes `654003fe` and the earlier merge of `main` at `a7dbf693`. v0.7.1 versions are kept wherever main set them, and the Intel carrier stays removed (main's v0.7.1 bump of `npm/platforms/darwin-x64/package.json` was resolved by keeping the deletion; `npm/cli/package.json` carries 0.7.1 for the launcher and its four carriers). Counts come from workflow declarations and executable contract modeling, not hosted release execution. The baseline release workflow built both Darwin architectures but did **not** contain a Rosetta installation proof.\n\n| Workflow/call | Triggering events | Before Mac jobs/run | After Mac jobs/run |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `ci.yml` | Ordinary PR opened/synchronize/reopened | 2: check and install-path matrix rows | 1: combined proofs |\n| `ci.yml` | Same-repository `release-plz-` PR with semantic version/changelog-only changes | 2 | 0: classifier-authorized omission |\n| `ci.yml` | Push to `main`, including ordinary and release-PR merges | 0 when the old helper proved the tree; 2 on fallback | 0: fallback and helper removed |\n| `ci.yml` | `workflow_dispatch` | Not a trigger | 0 by default; 1 with explicit diagnostic opt-in, outside the lifecycle |\n| `release.yml` | `release: published` | 1, building x86_64 Darwin (**removed**) and aarch64 Darwin | 1, building and natively proving aarch64 Darwin only |\n| `visual-docs.yml` → pinned screencomp v0.4.8 reusable workflow | PR opened/synchronize/reopened/closed, `main` push, schedule | 0 | 0 |\n| `live-janitor.yml` | Schedule, `workflow_dispatch` | 0 | 0 |\n| `notignored.yml` | `pull_request` | 0 | 0 |\n| `release-plz.yml` | `main` push | 0 | 0 |\n\nRelease-tag pushes, downstream `workflow_run`, `repository_dispatch`, `merge_group` and schedules request no Mac. The modeled automatic lifecycle spends Mac runners only on ordinary PR CI and the release build: **2 runs, at most 1 Mac job each**.\n\nLinux carriers retain the exact names `check (macos-latest)` and `install path (macos-latest)`. They use `always()` and explicit prerequisite outcomes, reject failed/cancelled/missing required work, and report authorized omission without claiming tests ran. The existing `check (ubuntu-latest)`, `check (windows-latest)`, `install path (ubuntu-latest)`, `install path (windows-latest)`, `deny`, `llmlint`, `pr-title` and `visual-docs / report (x86_64, shots/current, shots/verify, Visual docs)` contexts remain.\n\n### Release compatibility\n\n| Platform | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| x86_64 Linux GNU | Archive/checksum, CLI wheel, `cli-linux-x64` carrier | Unchanged |\n| aarch64 Linux GNU | Archive/checksum, CLI wheel, `cli-linux-arm64` carrier | Unchanged |\n| x86_64 Windows MSVC | ZIP/checksum, CLI wheel, `cli-win32-x64` carrier | Unchanged |\n| aarch64 Darwin | Archive/checksum, CLI wheel, `cli-darwin-arm64` carrier | Retained; built and installed natively in one Mac job |\n| x86_64 Darwin | Archive/checksum, CLI wheel, `cli-darwin-x64` carrier | **Discontinued** |\n\nEach target's wheel payload supplies its archive and npm carrier. Verification compares payload hashes, architecture, version, tags and contents; native installation and execution precede publication. Release-asset attachment and registry publication run on Linux. The Mac release job contains no Intel cross-compilation or Rosetta step.\n\nOn Intel macOS, `scripts/install.sh` exits 69 and the npm launcher exits 64 with “Intel macOS is no longer supported.” Windows Bash installation converts `file:///C:/...` URLs into usable drive-letter paths. Git Bash discovery also resolves installations behind PATH shims through git's `--exec-path`.\n\n### Routing and contract evidence\n\nThe private, locked `github-workflows` Nx project expands actual workflow matrices, evaluates conditions using the published Actions expression library, traverses pinned reusable calls and follows event fan-out and exact-head/tag artifact needs. Unresolved calls or runner expressions fail explicitly.\n\nThe production classifier permits release-only omission only for a same-repository `release-plz-` branch with a parsed version/changelog-only diff. Author identity is not authority. Subprocess journeys cover bot identities, forged titles/branches, fork heads, mixed release changes, malformed input and same-named registry dependencies distinguished by source. Unreadable classifications and unknown event names require Mac coverage; known non-PR automatic events remain Mac-free. Manual opt-in is handled separately by workflow routing.\n\nThe workload covers 12 event classes, three diff classes, two ownership classes, eight optional-publish combinations, every retained release architecture and 48 single-push lifecycles. Uncached tests record source-digested telemetry in `.github/.telemetry/macos-policy.json`; reporters reject missing/stale telemetry and never rerun scenarios. The registered budgets are `onetaskgraph-macos-jobs-per-run` and `onetaskgraph-macos-runs-per-change`. Their separate bounds protect against both several occupied slots within one run and repeated Mac-spending runs across a change.\n\n### Recorded local verification\n\nAt finished head `a31084f1` (merge of main v0.7.1), all run locally on Linux on 2026-10-16 UTC:\n\n- `github-workflows` format-check, lint, typecheck, test and budgets (`--skip-nx-cache`): passed; `node --test .github/tests/*.test.mjs` **54/54 passed**; onebudgetspec: **1 job/run against budget 1; 2 runs/change against budget 2; both within**.\n- `bash scripts/set-version.sh --check`, `check-distribution-contract.sh`, `check-distribution-contract-enforced.sh`, `check-release-targets.sh`, `check-release-packaging.sh`, `check-release-pr-sync.sh`: all passed.\n- `onetaskgraph:build` then `bash scripts/test-distribution.sh`: passed. That journey builds, packs, installs and runs the real Linux x86_64 product through production commands at 0.7.1, including wheel extraction, Intel refusal and the Windows file-URL conversion fixture.\n- `scripts:test` through `./scripts/nx.sh`: passed. A first attempt launched through `npx nx` failed in `check-relative-interpreter.sh` → `test-distribution.sh`'s authenticated publish to the loopback npm registry with `ENEEDAUTH`. The cause was the invocation: `npx` exports `npm_config_userconfig=~/.npmrc`, which overrides the journey's `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG`. The repository's own wrapper sets no such variable, and the rerun through it passed.\n- actionlint over `ci.yml` and `release.yml`: clean. The merge changed neither file.\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/main` (base `31392146`), through the repository recipe with no harness override: **33 passed, 0 failed, 13 skipped, 2 ignored, 8 not relevant**, report `20261016T053711Z-37489`, judged by the primary harness, codex `gpt-6.1-sol` (per oneharness history; no fallback to claude-code).\n\nEarlier evidence, superseded by the runs above where they overlap:\n\nAt finished head `b7e72bea`, after the packaging-guard repair:\n\n- `node --test .github/tests/*.test.mjs`: **54/54 passed**.\n- `bash scripts/check-release-packaging.sh`: passed. Restoring the previous `[^ ]+` pair regex induced the hosted Windows refusal on Linux: `invalid npm platform identifier`. That induced failure was reverted.\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/main`, against `a7dbf693`: **33 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored**, report `20261015T155711Z-5b6a1`, through the repository recipe with no harness override.\n\n`b7e72bea` changes only `scripts/check-release-packaging.sh`. The remaining `cddae191` checks below do not read that changed guard; the workflow suite and packaging check were rerun above.\n\nAt `cddae191`:\n\n- `node --test .github/tests/*.test.mjs`: **54/54 passed**.\n- `bash scripts/test-distribution.sh` and `bash scripts/check-release-packaging.sh`: passed. The distribution journey builds, packs, installs and runs the real Linux x86_64 product through production commands, including wheel extraction, Intel refusal and Windows file-URL conversion fixtures.\n- Biome format/lint and `tsc -p .github/tsconfig.json`: clean.\n- `just lint-llm-diff main`, against `a7dbf693`: **33 passed, 0 failed**, report `20261015T144012Z-d96a6`, using the repository recipe without a harness override.\n- `NX_DAEMON=false ./scripts/nx.sh run github-workflows:budgets --skip-nx-cache`: exited 0, rerunning its test dependency because both changed files were telemetry digest inputs. The regenerated digest was `fc8992ce991a1a76fbbf98cea54fa5cf63426f3c95803248b5a9a2842e088424`; the subsequent packaging-guard repair does not change those digest inputs.\n- `bun run onebudgetspec check .github/budgets.yaml`: **1 job/run against budget 1; 2 runs/change against budget 2; both within**. Both metric commands returned those figures and exited 0.\n\nThe following earlier results remain applicable: the later changes to `scripts/release_products.py`, `.github/tests/release.test.mjs` and `scripts/check-release-packaging.sh` do not change these graph guards' or actionlint's inputs.\n\n- At `be7ca159`, `scripts/check-nx-graph.sh`, `scripts/check-workspace-config.sh`, `scripts/check-live-seat-serialised.sh` and `scripts/check-affected-selection.sh` passed.\n- At `be7ca159`, actionlint over changed `ci.yml` and `release.yml` was clean. The earlier all-workflow pass was at `654003fe`; the intervening merge changed `ci.yml`, which was checked again.\n\nAdditional historical evidence:\n\n- At `be7ca159`, all 54 workflow tests and both distribution/packaging checks passed. The wheel extractor's path-refusal case failed against both the original extractor and intermediate suffix-only validation. Both budget reporters refused stale telemetry before regeneration; the later budget results above supersede those measurements.\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/main` at `be7ca159`, against `a7dbf693`: **33 passed, 0 failed**, report `20261015T135759Z-cf9ad`; `just lint-llm-validate` also passed. At `654003fe`, against `31c5e024`, judged lint recorded **32 passed, 0 failed**, report `20261014T125819Z-5e6a7`.\n- Earlier merges `485ac59c` and `76451318` retained main's package versions while keeping four carriers and removing the Intel carrier; version and distribution-contract checks passed after each. The final merge retains the live-seat serialization guard and removes the retired Mac-selection guard.\n\nThe finished configuration names `gpt-6.1-sol` in `oneharness.toml`, `llmlint.yml` and setup-script commentary. Lint findings also led to removal of unnecessary staging credentials, stricter wheel-extractor path validation, corrected comments and budget wording, and the scoped exceptions below.\n\nLocal execution establishes Linux behavior. Darwin and Windows execution is evidenced only by the hosted observations below; release execution remains contract-level evidence.\n\n### Hosted draft observations\n\nThese are historical snapshots of [draft #3601](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3601), not current-status claims. **No completed hosted result for `b7e72bea` or finished head `a31084f1` is recorded here; the `a31084f1` row is an in-progress snapshot.** Release-only PRs, pushes, schedules, downstream fan-out and release publication were modeled rather than observed.\n\n| Snapshot UTC / exact head | CI evidence | Other workflows |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `663eecb2` | [38404336812](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38404336812): one Mac job failed; both Mac-name carriers correctly failed. Ubuntu/Windows checks and Windows install path also failed; subsequent repairs are described below. | Visual docs and notignored succeeded. |\n| 2026-10-14 03:01 / `63156e42` | [38503959174](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38503959174): queued overall; sole Mac job queued; classification, `pr-title` and `deny` succeeded; other check/install lanes and llmlint in progress. Mac-name carriers had not yet been created. | [Visual docs](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38503959340) in progress; [notignored](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38503959095) succeeded. |\n| 2026-10-14 04:37 / `63156e42` | Same CI run completed with failure. Mac job, both carriers, Ubuntu check/install, classification, `deny` and `pr-title` succeeded. Windows check/install failed on a missing-file diagnostic; llmlint failed on the release job name. Both were repaired at `693ad19f`. `github-workflows:test` passed on Windows. | The linked Visual docs and notignored runs succeeded. |\n| 2026-10-14 04:38 / `693ad19f` | [38512389231](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38512389231): queued, no job results yet. | [Visual docs](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38512389456) and [notignored](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38512389146) in progress. |\n| 2026-10-14 14:2x / `693ad19f`, superseded | Same CI run completed with failure. Mac job, both carriers and every other job except Windows check succeeded. That Windows failure was not investigated in the recorded work after this head was superseded. | — |\n| 2026-10-14 14:19 / `654003fe` | [38567998684](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38567998684): failed overall. Classification required Mac. The sole Mac job queued from 12:59–13:03, then succeeded at 14:18; both carriers succeeded. Both install-path lanes, `deny`, `pr-title` and llmlint succeeded. Ubuntu/Windows checks failed as detailed below. | [Visual docs](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38567999208) queued at 12:59, then succeeded; [notignored](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38567998554) succeeded. |\n| 2026-10-15 14:34 / `be7ca159` | [38749647097](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38749647097): [Windows install path](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38749647097/job/116472558892) failed in `test-release-products.py` with “Git Bash could not be found beside git” on runner image `windows-2025-vs2026` 20261007.264.1. The step passed at `654003fe` on image 20260925.250.1 with no intervening resolver change. Repaired at `cddae191`; other jobs were still running at this snapshot. | — |\n| 2026-10-15 15:50 / `cddae191` | [38754138567](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38754138567): classification, `pr-title`, `deny`, llmlint and both Ubuntu/Windows install-path lanes succeeded; the Windows Git Bash repair held. The sole Mac job was still in progress. [Ubuntu check](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38754138567/job/116489917588) failed only in the live GitHub Projects journey `real_projects_v2_contract_writes_and_leaves_no_residue`: “GitHub gave the project no change token after its native far end deleted, though the leg waited 30 seconds past the plugin's settling margin”. Windows check failed in `scripts:distribution-check`, where the packaging guard's Windows-only branch read the Darwin `TARGETS` pair with `[^ ]+` and captured the newline; repaired at `b7e72bea`. | — |\n| 2026-10-16 05:38 / `a31084f1` | [38856794975](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38856794975): in progress. `pr-title`, `deny` and the `macOS lanes` classification succeeded; the sole Mac job `macOS check and install proofs`, both Ubuntu/Windows check and install-path lanes and llmlint were in progress, and the Mac-name carriers had not yet been created. | [notignored](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38856794920) succeeded; [Visual docs](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38856795245) in progress. |\n\nRepairs following `663eecb2` cover ANSI-colored Node errors, Windows path separators in classifier version-file keys, UTF-8 subprocess decoding, Git Bash resolution instead of the WSL launcher, resolved macOS temporary-directory paths and Windows drive-letter file URLs. Color-on/color-off, simulated Windows path spelling, symlinked temporary directories and a MINGW file-URL fixture reproduced applicable failures locally. The WSL launcher case was not reproduced on Linux; a Windows-layout resolver test covers that branch. Missing-checksum diagnostics now identify the missing archive checksum without depending on POSIX versus Windows error wording. The non-Mac release job was renamed `native-assets-carriers-and-wheels`; no protected name changed.\n\nAt `cddae191`, Git Bash discovery additionally uses git's `--exec-path` and a bounded ancestor search for `bin/bash.exe` or `usr/bin/bash.exe`. Linux-run tests cover a PATH shim outside the installation and a shim naming no installation, which still refuses. The new shim case failed against the previous resolver. The subsequent hosted Windows install-path success is recorded in the table; hosted execution of the final packaging-guard repair remains unobserved here.\n\nThis branch changes no crate. The whole graph is selected because the diff deletes `npm/platforms/darwin-x64/package.json`, which Nx treats as touching every project, measured with `nx show projects --affected --files=…`. That deletion is required by the Intel discontinuation, so this branch runs both live lanes. At `cddae191`, the live GitHub Projects failure concerned GitHub's change-token timing on the shared board, outside the code changed here; the journey and its bounds were not altered and the job was not rerun.\n\nAt `654003fe`, Ubuntu's live GitHub Projects journey refused the shared board's **91 items and 14 fields**, outside its registered **51–90 item** workload; main had passed the same journey at 12:45 that day. Windows' loopback `cache_budget` journey reported **os error 10055**, insufficient socket buffer space. These failures were outside the changed Rust code; workload bounds were not relaxed and those hosted jobs were not rerun in the recorded work. The moved Mac proofs and both Linux/Windows installation lanes passed.\n\n### Scoped lint exceptions\n\nThis inventory covers directives added, rewritten or removed by the diff and existing site directives covering changed lines:\n\n- `.github/budgets.yaml`: two `budgets_track_product_owner_outcomes` sites document the approved separate scheduling bounds; two `budget_commands_measure_directly` sites retain the fixed telemetry-reporting interface. `.github/macos-budget.mjs` has one corresponding command-interface exception over its metric allowlist. Reporters consume recorded telemetry without rerunning work.\n- `.github/reusable/screencomp-v0.4.8.yml`: generated-fixture exceptions for `boundary_inputs_validated` and `comments_earn_their_place` preserve pinned upstream content; its upstream `changed_behavior_has_e2e` file annotation is retained.\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: the combined Mac step's `live_tier_compiles_and_requires_credential` and `no_second_broader_sweep_over_an_already_gated_commit` block explains Linux-only live credentials and the permitted manual diagnostic. The old main-push fallback exception is removed.\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: the existing `changed_behavior_has_e2e` publication block covers changed build/proof steps, targets, ZIP packaging and staging-token removal. Packaging and native Linux installation are exercised without publishing; real publication is not claimed.\n- `.github/package.json`, `.github/project.json`, `.github/tsconfig.json` and `.github/bun.lock`: four `projects_stay_in_one_js_workspace` file annotations explain the required isolated private tooling package.\n- `.github/semantic-release.py`, `scripts/test-release-products.py` and `scripts/verify-release-products.py`: three `async_typed_clients_at_boundaries` file annotations cover sequential local subprocesses rather than hosted-service clients.\n- `scripts/release-wheel-binary.py`: two `async_typed_clients_at_boundaries` sites cover synchronous wheel discovery and ZIP reading in an ordered release step. `scripts/release_products.py` has two sites for reading the local workflow as the tag grammar's authority.\n- `scripts/verify-release-products.py`: five `changed_behavior_has_e2e` sites cover venv, pip, npm and CLI version/help execution. Real native installation exercises successful execution, while a real installer failure drives the shared failure handler. The earlier Darwin/Rosetta exception was removed with that path.\n- `scripts/test-release-products.py`: one `changed_behavior_has_e2e` site explains the explicit write mode of the malformed carrier-manifest fixture; the journey exercises refusal and recovery.\n- `npm/cli/bin/onetaskgraph.js`: the rewritten platform-mapping `changed_behavior_has_e2e` exception names only the unavailable Linux ARM64 runner. Intel refusal is exercised by the distribution journey.\n- `npm/cli/package.json`: the rewritten `projects_stay_in_one_js_workspace` file annotation explains four publication carriers and five synchronized versions; workspace linking would resolve empty, unbuilt carrier directories.\n- Removed with their code: the Intel carrier's `projects_stay_in_one_js_workspace` annotation, the installer's Darwin x64 `changed_behavior_has_e2e` site and the retired selection helper's `tool_output_is_signal` block. The installer's Linux ARM64 site and `scripts/project.json` file annotation remain unchanged.\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:18:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T06:59:22Z","closed_at":"2026-10-16T06:59:20Z","merged_at":"2026-10-16T06:59:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"f178102159bd7c231641fe804e47cbb6472cd024","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3601/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3601/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3601/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/a31084f146558c3f99e9e122bfe5a222feea8ea6","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/3596/macos-onetaskgraph","ref":"nick/3596/macos-onetaskgraph","sha":"a31084f146558c3f99e9e122bfe5a222feea8ea6","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1343250630,"node_id":"R_kgDOUBBgxg","name":"onetaskgraph","full_name":"nickderobertis/onetaskgraph","private":false,"owner":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph","description":"Unified SDK and C