":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3607"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3607"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3607/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3607/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3607/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/88ea6256ed6577d96882c602cefed00ec3abd721"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3604","id":4843661698,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUBBgxs8AAAABILRpgg","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3604","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3604.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pull/3604.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3604","number":3604,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"perf(github-live): keep the complete live lane below 300 GraphQL points","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nReduce the complete GitHub live lane’s workload while retaining real-board, fresh-token and asset-copy assertions. Account for both journeys, retries and cleanup, and enforce the `github-live-session-points` budget at 299 points; stale or incomplete telemetry cannot pass.\n\nAccept shared boards with 51–90 initial items, including the observed 84-item board, and identify the actual population in each bill. Preserve earlier telemetry during repeat collection and repair Windows launch, text decoding and loopback executable discovery.\n\n## Why\n\nSeveral hosts share one GitHub account’s hourly allowance. Keeping each complete live session under 300 GraphQL points preserves quota for other work and reduces quota refusals that delay merges.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe retained complete live pair measured **212 attributed points on 90 initial items**: 146 response-reported query points plus 66 explicitly modelled mutation points, leaving **87 points headroom** against 299. Both journeys completed owned cleanup, and all 14 unconditional token transitions passed with the real settling margin. The [measurement, coverage matrix and pricing qualifications](crates/onetaskgraph-github-projects/tests/fixtures/session-cost.md) and [machine-produced budget result](crates/onetaskgraph-github-projects/tests/fixtures/live-session-20261013/onebudgetspec-result.json) identify measured revision `ca86536a98dfe5a412598e3b4adac1749da228af`. No measured before/after savings are claimed.\n\nThe accepted population now has explicit bounds:\n\n- **51 minimum:** the whole-board task walk requests pages of 50 and needs a second page to exercise cursor traversal and cross-page duplicate assertions. Other assertions over existing board items need at most one. Item count is a necessary bound, not a guarantee of task composition.\n- **90 maximum:** this is the population used for the retained 212-point measurement; larger boards are unmeasured. The journey still requires exactly 14 fields and unchanged fixture facts, and refuses outside the range before setup, naming the observed count and bounds.\n\nThe registered threshold and measured workload record are unchanged. Bills identify their observed population and explicitly distinguish a smaller board from the registered 90-item measurement. The loopback pair completes on 84 items and passes the registered budget; 50- and 91-item boards are refused before writes and cannot produce a bill. Restoring exact-match billing makes the 84-item regression fail.\n\nRepeat collection exclusively creates the first unused sibling of `target/debug/telemetry/github-live-session/<run-id>-<attempt>`, from `.2` through `.100`, preserving earlier records and excluding them from the new bill. Local runs default to a UUID identity. The repaired recipe checks reach both distribution targets, including when the original telemetry directory contains a sentinel.\n\nThe decline guard now expects the recheck’s current wording without weakening its quota assertion. The earlier [Windows merge-path run](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38458328058/job/115506699678) passed the plugin test target but exposed loopback executable discovery’s forward-slash-only matcher; discovery now accepts either host separator, and fixture readiness is published atomically. Absolute Git Bash/Git/Bun resolution, MSYS-runtime identification, strict UTF-8 selection decoding and forwarding, ASCII Git object-name decoding, and blocking accepted loopback sockets remain in force. The forced-cp1252 regression proves the em-dash round-trip and failure propagation, and fails with either encoding repair reverted.\n\nThe [offline verification report and retained evidence](crates/onetaskgraph-github-projects/tests/fixtures/verification-20261013/README.md) preserve the earlier comparisons and checks, including `0bc6a76c` → `20562737`, the comparison from `2f23f8f6`, and `615d7019` → `e5e9532b` and `4839f622`. The latest comparison drove both actual live entry points on a 90-item loopback board at `d22c0322` and executable tree `0406e092`: identical normalized **193 HTTP operations**, including **174 GraphQL requests**, byte-identical prices, and the same **174-point bill** (108 reported + 66 modelled). Reporter detail adds the board population; dynamic request payloads are not claimed byte-identical. The 84-item fixture also bills 174 points because its queries each cost one fixture point; this is not a real-GitHub measurement.\n\nLinux verification recorded 625 passing tests across the three changed crates, including all nine `recheck_gate` tests and eleven loopback-pair tests; credentialed journeys printed their skips. Relative-interpreter, lane-selection, budget-decline, fixture and encoding guards passed, as did workspace formatting, Rust formatting and clippy over all targets/features of the changed crates with warnings denied. Head `d0738a90` adds verification documentation, with workspace formatting checked afterward. The report retains earlier doctest, scripts-project and serial SDK results, including the separately recorded concurrent packaging race. No new live GitHub session ran during these repairs, and no successful Windows merge-path run of the final repair is claimed.\n\nThe [earlier Linux merge-path failure](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38465257225/job/115530262511) observed 84 items and 14 fields and refused the former exact-90 requirement; this change addresses that refusal. The report retains the inference that scheduled cleanup removed six abandoned fixture items, without claiming item-level attribution. The [later Ubuntu run](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/actions/runs/38470377878/job/115547891047) declined because the shared allowance was insufficient; that admission behavior remains correct and unchanged.","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:04:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:26Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:24Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T22:51:24Z","merge_commit_sha":"9400269df0519947b32bba815edbfd2a54b43d42","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3604/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/3604/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/issues/3604/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/statuses/d0738a90c13072c62124bf7d5c880ea3c5b3df4a","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/3602/reduce-live-session","ref":"nick/3602/reduce-live-session","sha":"d0738a90c13072c62124bf7d5c880ea3c5b3df4a","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1343250630,"node_id":"R_kgDOUBBgxg","name":"onetaskgraph","full_name":"nickderobertis/onetaskgraph","private":false,"owner":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph","description":"Unified SDK and CLI for project-management ticketing systems: a Rust core with a plugin interface, Python and TypeScript wrappers, and pluggable task sources (local Markdown, Linear, GitHub Projects, in-memory).","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/collaborator